# Code Conventions

## Line Length
- Maximum 100 characters per line
- Break long lines at logical points

## Imports and Props (3+ items)
- **Imports:** When an import has 3 or more named items, break into multiple lines (one item per line).
- **Props:** When a component receives 3 or more props (or destructuring has 3+ keys), put each on its own line for readability.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD - 3+ items on one line
import { staggerContainer, staggerItem, fadeInUp } from '../../styles/animations';
<Button variant="primary" size="md" onClick={handleClick} aria-label="Submit" />

// ✅ GOOD - one per line
import {
  staggerContainer,
  staggerItem,
  fadeInUp,
} from '../../styles/animations';
<Button
  variant="primary"
  size="md"
  onClick={handleClick}
  aria-label="Submit"
/>
```

## Language
- All comments in English
- All variable/function/class names in English

## Functions

### Single Responsibility
Each function must have only one responsibility and one return type.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD - mixed responsibilities
function getUserData(id: string) {
  const user = db.findUser(id);
  sendEmail(user.email); // side effect
  return user;
}

// ✅ GOOD - single responsibility
function getUserById(id: string): User {
  return db.findUser(id);
}

function notifyUser(user: User): void {
  sendEmail(user.email);
}
```

### Self-Documenting with Comments
Functions must be self-explanatory with clear comments describing functionality.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD - no documentation
function calc(a, b) {
  return a * b * 0.1;
}

// ✅ GOOD - documented and clear
/**
 * Calculates the discount amount based on price and quantity.
 * Applies a 10% discount rate.
 */
function calculateDiscount(price: number, quantity: number): number {
  const DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.1;
  return price * quantity * DISCOUNT_RATE;
}
```
